low`` exception when the magnitude of :math:`x` is the largest\n51\t * finite value representable in the type and :math:`y` is infinite with the\n52\t * same sign as :math:`x`.\n53\t *\n54\t * .. May raise ``underflow`` exception.\n55\t *\n56\t * Output map\n57\t * ==========\n58\t *\n59\t * +--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+\n60\t * | nexttoward(x,y)          | x                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n61\t * +--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------+\n62\t * | y                        | :math:`-Inf`             | :math:`<0`               | :math:`-0`               | :math:`+0`               | :math:`>0`               | :math:`+Inf`             | :math:`NaN`              |\n63\t * +==========================+==========================+==========================+==========================+==========================+==========================+==========================+==========================+\n64\t * | :math:`-Inf`             | :math:`-Inf`             | :math:`nexttoward(x, y)` | max :math:`\\mathbb{S}^{-}`                          | :math:`nexttoward(x, y)` | :math:`nexttoward(x, y)` | :math:`qNaN`             |\n65\t * +--------------------------+--------------------------+                          +                                                     +                          +                          +                          +\n66\t * | :math:`<0`               | :math:`nexttoward(x, y)` |                          |                                          